+# Semper — Terms of Service
+
+**Last updated:** 2026-08-05  
+**Product:** Semper (IndicVision DIC)
+
+These Terms govern use of the Semper Android application and any optional cloud
+sync backend operated with it. By signing in or using cloud features, you agree
+to these Terms. If you do not agree, do not use the cloud features; offline
+analysis may still be available depending on your build.
+
+## 1. The service
+
+Semper performs digital image correlation / related analysis **on the device**.
+Optional cloud features provide identity, metadata storage (Firestore), artifact
+storage (Google Drive Shared Drive), sync, restore, and admin access control.
+There is **no** generative AI / LLM feature in this product.
+
+## 2. Accounts and access
+
+- Access may require Firebase Authentication and operator approval (PENDING →
+  APPROVED). Operators may suspend accounts.
+- You must keep credentials secure. Device attestation binds an account to a
+  registered device; transferring devices may require re-registration per
+  product rules.
+- You are responsible for activity under your account.
+
+## 3. Acceptable use
+
+You may not: attempt to bypass authentication or attestation; abuse rate limits
+or quotas; upload unlawful content; interfere with other users; reverse-engineer
+the service except where mandatory law allows; or use the service to process
+data you are not authorized to handle.
+
+## 4. Your content
+
+You retain rights to analysis data you create. By syncing, you grant the
+operator a limited license to store and process that data solely to provide
+sync, restore, support, and security. Cloud quotas and file-size limits apply.
+
+## 5. Privacy
+
+Personal data is described in the [Privacy Policy](PRIVACY_POLICY.md). Export and
+deletion capabilities and their limits are part of that policy.
+
+## 6. Availability and disclaimers
+
+The service is provided **“as is”**. Offline-first design means core measurement
+work can continue when cloud is unavailable; sync may be delayed. We do not
+warrant uninterrupted cloud availability. To the maximum extent permitted by
+law, liability for cloud features is limited to direct damages not exceeding
+fees paid (if any) for the service in the prior three months — or zero if the
+service is provided without charge.
+
+## 7. Research / professional use
+
+Results are tools for engineering/research workflows. You are responsible for
+validation, calibration, and decisions made from outputs.
+
+## 8. Termination
+
+You may stop using the app and request account deletion. Operators may suspend
+or terminate access for breach or risk. Survival: sections on content license
+(for residual backups), disclaimers, liability limits, and audit retention.
+
+## 9. Changes
+
+Terms may be updated; continued use after notice constitutes acceptance where
+permitted. Material changes should appear in release notes or in-app notice.
+
+## 10. Contact
+
+Support / help from the app settings, or the deployment’s configured support
+email.
+
+## 11. Governing law
+
+Replace with the deploying organization’s chosen jurisdiction before public
+distribution. Until then, these Terms are a **template** for operator review.
